# StudyStreak: rules for every coding agent

You work on one task file at a time from `tasks/`. Read `docs/PRD.md` and `docs/DESIGN.md` first.

## Stack
- Next.js 15 (App Router, TypeScript)
- Tailwind CSS
- localStorage only

## Folder layout
- app/ holds Next.js App Router pages and layout
- components/ holds all React components
- lib/ holds storage.ts, date.ts, streak.ts utilities
- __tests__/ holds Jest test files

## Conventions
- Use TypeScript with strict mode
- All components are functional with proper props typing
- Tailwind classes for all styling, mobile-first
- localStorage keys are 'habits' and 'completions'
- No network calls or external dependencies
- Dates always in YYYY-MM-DD format via lib/date.ts
- Every component must be accessible (ARIA labels, keyboard nav)

## Commands
- install: `npm install`
- dev: `npm run dev`
- test: `npm test`
- build: `npm run build`

## Never
- Never commit secrets or API keys
- Never add backend, auth, or network requests
- Never touch files outside the current task
- Never exceed 5 habits
- Never add presets, onboarding tooltip, or history >7 days
- Never write real secret values or env vars
- Never commit secrets, API keys or `.env` files; read configuration from environment variable names.
- Never change files outside the current task's scope.
- Open one PR per task titled `[task-NNN] <title>` with `Part of #<issue number>` in the description.
